From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knapcio <knapcio@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:16:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] DSel: drafting-cost overrides G6_S2_DSEL_DCOST / _MCOST
 / _MEACH

Unset keeps 5.6 + 2.5, 2.5 + 3.0 and 2.1 ms; the rank-0 drafter-choice line
prints the values in use.
---
 docs/SETTINGS.md       |  2 +-
 engine/runtime/g6m4.cu | 10 ++++++++--
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/SETTINGS.md b/docs/SETTINGS.md
index 9f49e7d..585e78d 100644
--- a/docs/SETTINGS.md
+++ b/docs/SETTINGS.md
@@ -93,7 +93,7 @@ the short version.
 | `G6_GV_MULTI` | 1 | steps of up to 8 rows run the GEMVs on the layer input (q_a, kv_a, the indexer's k and weights) as one launch; 0 = one launch each (same bits) |
 | `G6_S2_ADAPT` | 0 | S2: choose each round's MTP draft count (1..k) from the sessions' accept rates and the S2 step costs; 1 adds ~1 GiB of main-step graphs |
 | `G6_S2_GROW` | 1 | S2: a session below R holds the KV pages it needs now and takes more as its output grows, admitted and grown only while every live session can still reach prompt + `max_tokens` + guard; a session that cannot grow sits out rounds. 0 = every run holds that worst case from admission |
-| `G6_S2_DSEL` | 1 | S2 with DFlash2: a request that decodes alone drafts each round with DFlash2 or MTP, whichever is expected to commit more tokens per ms (prose +4.5% on RigMark, code level); 0 = DFlash2 every round. `G6_S2_DSEL_MARGIN` (0.15), `G6_S2_DSEL_DWELL` (8 rounds) and `G6_S2_DSEL_PROBE` (4) tune it |
+| `G6_S2_DSEL` | 1 | S2 with DFlash2: a request that decodes alone drafts each round with DFlash2 or MTP, whichever is expected to commit more tokens per ms (prose +4.5% on RigMark, code level); 0 = DFlash2 every round. `G6_S2_DSEL_MARGIN` (0.15), `G6_S2_DSEL_DWELL` (8 rounds) and `G6_S2_DSEL_PROBE` (4) tune it; `G6_S2_DSEL_DCOST` (8.1), `G6_S2_DSEL_MCOST` (5.5) and `G6_S2_DSEL_MEACH` (2.1) override its drafting ms per round (DFlash2; MTP's first form and the drafter's context step; each MTP chain step) |
 | `G6_S2_DSEL_START` | dflash | S2 drafter choice: `mtp` = a DFlash2 request starts on MTP (the drafter's prompt-tail drafts are its first probe) and moves to DFlash2 when the evidence says so. Every rank must set the same value |
 | `G6_S2_DSEL_POSCLK` | 0 | S2 drafter choice: 1 = its DFlash2 and MTP estimates decay a draft position only on rounds that observe it, so the DFlash2 rounds (which score MTP's first draft alone) no longer age MTP's later positions toward the seed. Every rank must set the same value |
 | `G6_DEC_EVPROF` | unset | measurement: N = per-stage decode step times from event nodes in the captured main-step graphs, printed every N main steps (rank logs) |
diff --git a/engine/runtime/g6m4.cu b/engine/runtime/g6m4.cu
index ca307d8..649026c 100644
--- a/engine/runtime/g6m4.cu
+++ b/engine/runtime/g6m4.cu
@@ -1169,8 +1169,14 @@ int main(int argc, char** argv)
                 h.dsel.d.draft_round = 5.6 + 2.5;
                 h.dsel.m.draft_round = 2.5 + 3.0;
                 h.dsel.m.draft_each = 2.1;
-                if (R == 0 && h.dsel.on) fprintf(stderr, "# s2 drafter choice on: DFlash2 or MTP per round (dwell %d, margin %.2f, probe %d)\n",
-                                                    h.dsel.dwell, h.dsel.margin, h.dsel.probe);
+                // the drafting ms above, overridden (A/B of the cost model; every rank the same values)
+                if (const char* e = getenv("G6_S2_DSEL_DCOST")) h.dsel.d.draft_round = atof(e);
+                if (const char* e = getenv("G6_S2_DSEL_MCOST")) h.dsel.m.draft_round = atof(e);
+                if (const char* e = getenv("G6_S2_DSEL_MEACH")) h.dsel.m.draft_each = atof(e);
+                if (R == 0 && h.dsel.on) fprintf(stderr, "# s2 drafter choice on: DFlash2 or MTP per round (dwell %d, margin %.2f, probe %d, "
+                                                    "drafting ms: DFlash2 %.2f, MTP %.2f + %.2f per chain step)\n",
+                                                    h.dsel.dwell, h.dsel.margin, h.dsel.probe, h.dsel.d.draft_round, h.dsel.m.draft_round,
+                                                    h.dsel.m.draft_each);
                 if (R == 0 && h.dsel.on && h.dsel.start_mtp) fprintf(stderr, "# s2 drafter choice: requests start on MTP\n");
                 if (R == 0 && h.dsel.on && h.dsel.posclk) fprintf(stderr, "# s2 drafter choice: per-position clocks\n");
                 // a 1-token prompt has no prefill: the drafter starts from its prompt step (dfl_lo = first, as plain)
